<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Värmland</h1><p class="st-meta">700 CE – 1000 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Forested petty kingdom north of Lake Vänern, known mostly from the Norse sagas, later absorbed into the Swedish realm.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Värmland, the land around the rivers flowing into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-vanern">Lake Vänern</a>, is known mainly from Icelandic sagas written centuries later. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/snorri-sturluson">Snorri Sturluson's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ynglinga-saga">Ynglinga saga</a> tells that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olof-tratalja">Olof the Tree-Feller</a>, driven from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala">Uppsala</a>, cleared the forests here and founded a new line of kings.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its people lived by farming, iron extraction from bog ore and forest trades, and met at their own assemblies. The sagas describe Värmland as a borderland contested by Norwegian, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/svear">Svear</a> and Geatish kings, with local kings or jarls of uncertain historical reality.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By around 1000 Värmland was drawn into the orbit of the Swedish kings, although Norwegian rulers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olaf-ii-of-norway">Olaf Haraldsson</a> also tried to claim it. It became a province of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sweden">Kingdom of Sweden</a>, keeping its own law and lawman in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/varmland.jpg" alt="Värmland" width="320" height="729"><figcaption>Image: Lapplänning (highlighting by Lokal_Profil) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sverigekarta-Landskap_V%C3%A4rmland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>700 CE – 1000 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Norse paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Norse</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/sweden">Sweden</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Värmland, Wermland</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=850&amp;focus=varmland" aria-label="Värmland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4958 173 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Värmland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5278 429L5381 440"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5381 440h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5278 429h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5278 429h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=850&amp;focus=varmland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
